  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "f516fcfc-ab98-47c2-92cf-347b89ca10c9",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Java 9 Changes \n\n### New features\n\n1. Introduced Java Platform Module System _(Jigsaw Project)_.\n2. Private method in interfaces\n3. Try with resources with effectively final variable\n4. Diamond Operator with Anonymous classes\n5. `@SafeVarags` is allowed on top of private method also. \n    - Previously was allowed on top of static, final, protected & public methods.\n6. Flow APIs introduced in `java.util.concurrent` package\n    - `Publisher`\n    - `Subscriber`\n    - `Subscription`\n    - `Processor`\n7. `VarHandle` \n8. Introduced HttpClient as incubator, got standardized in Java 11.\n9. Completeable Future API changes\n10. Collection Factories\n11. Stream Enhancement\n12. Optional Enhancement\n8. Process API improvements\n\n\n### Performance improvements\n\n1. String indification\n2. Compact String\n```sh\n    java -XX:-CompactStrings MyApp\n```\n3. GIGC as default garbage collector, replacing CMS.\n\n```sh\n\n        java -XX:+UseG1GC           MyApp   # G1 (now default)\n        java -XX:+UseParallelGC     MyApp   # Parallel GC (was Java 8 default)\n        java -XX:+UseSerialGC       MyApp   # Serial GC\n        java -XX:+UseConcMarkSweepGC MyApp  # CMS (deprecated, removed in java 14)\n\n        java -XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200 \\     # target max pause\n        -XX:G1HeapRegionSize=16m \\     # region size\n        -XX:G1NewSizePercent=20 \\      # min young gen %\n        -XX:G1MaxNewSizePercent=40 MyApp\n```\n\n### Tools\n\n1. Introduced jShell REPL\n2. jlink to add only modules needed as per project\n\n```sh\n\n        jlink \\\n        --jpms-path $JAVA_HOME/jmods:mods \\\n        --add-modules com.myapp \\\n        --output myruntime \\\n        --compress=2 \\\n        --strip-debug \\\n        --no-header-files \\\n        --no-man-pages\n\n```\n\n3. Multirelease jar for different java runtimes\n\n```sh\n        # MANIFEST.MF must include:\n        Multi-Release: true\n\n        # Build with jar tool:\n        jar --create --file myapp.jar \\\n            --main-class com.myapp.Main \\\n            -C base-classes . \\\n            --release 9 -C java9-classes . \\\n            --release 11 -C java11-classes .\n```\n\n4. Unified Logging for JVM\n\n```sh\n        # Single -Xlog flag for all JVM logging\n        # Syntax: -Xlog[:[selectors][:[output][:[decorators][:output-options]]]]\n\n        java -Xlog:gc                   MyApp   # GC logs\n        java -Xlog:gc*                  MyApp   # GC + sub-tags\n        java -Xlog:gc:file=gc.log       MyApp   # to file\n        java -Xlog:gc+heap=debug        MyApp   # gc.heap at debug level\n        java -Xlog:all=debug:stdout     MyApp   # everything\n        java -Xlog:class+load=info      MyApp   # class loading\n\n        # Log levels: trace, debug, info, warning, error\n        # Decorators: time, uptime, timemillis, pid, tid, level, tags\n        java -Xlog:gc::time,uptime,pid  MyApp\n```",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "f516fcfc-ab98-47c2-92cf-347b89ca10c9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9ef60909-d06c-444b-9e63-6154d58fe009",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Interface Changes",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "9ef60909-d06c-444b-9e63-6154d58fe009"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "82d80bff-eb79-43f8-8e46-31f64932736a",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "interface Validator<T> {\r\n\r\n    boolean isValid(T value);\r\n\r\n    // Default method using private helper\r\n    default Validator<T> and(Validator<T> other) {\r\n        return value -> isValid(value) && other.isValid(value);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    default Validator<T> or(Validator<T> other) {\r\n        return value -> isValid(value) || other.isValid(value);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    default String validate(T value) {\r\n        return isValid(value) ? formatOk(value) : formatFail(value);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // private — shared by default methods, not visible to implementors\r\n    private String formatOk(T v)   { return \"✓ Valid: \" + v;   }\r\n    private String formatFail(T v) { return \"✗ Invalid: \" + v; }\r\n\r\n    // private static — utility not needing instance\r\n    private static boolean isNullOrEmpty(String s) {\r\n        return s == null || s.isEmpty();\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    static Validator<String> notEmpty() {\r\n        return s -> !isNullOrEmpty(s);  // uses private static\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Usage\r\nValidator<String> notEmpty = Validator.notEmpty();\r\nValidator<String> notTooLong = s -> s.length() <= 50;\r\nValidator<String> username = notEmpty.and(notTooLong);\r\n\r\nusername.validate(\"Alice\");  // \"✓ Valid: Alice\"\r\nusername.validate(\"\");       // \"✗ Invalid: \"",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "875e6fa6-3b3f-40c3-b6d2-1524d7b1ffe2",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Try With Resource changes",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "875e6fa6-3b3f-40c3-b6d2-1524d7b1ffe2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "45978b54-28ff-4665-87a6-6374f4c1aecd",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Java 7/8: had to re-declare effectively final variable in try()\r\nConnection conn = getConnection();\r\ntry (Connection c = conn) { // redundant re-declaration\r\n    c.doWork();\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Java 9: effectively final variable can be used directly\r\nConnection conn = getConnection(); // effectively final\r\ntry (conn) {                        // no re-declaration needed\r\n    conn.doWork();\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Multiple resources\r\nInputStream  in  = new FileInputStream(\"input.txt\");\r\nOutputStream out = new FileOutputStream(\"output.txt\");\r\ntry (in; out) {\r\n    in.transferTo(out);\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Mix of new and existing variables\r\nBufferedReader existing = getReader();\r\ntry (existing; BufferedWriter w = new BufferedWriter(...)) {\r\n    existing.lines().forEach(w::write);\r\n}",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "d048b0ba-d86a-45ef-81bc-40e769354103",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Anonymous Classes & Diamond operator",
