    {
      "id": "375699ed-7dae-442e-9ae9-d36688c2e90d",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Java 8: _ alone as variable name gave a warning\r\n// Java 9: compile ERROR — reserved for future use (pattern matching)\r\n\r\n// This now fails to compile:\r\n// String _ = \"unused\";  ← error in Java 9\r\n// int _ = getValue();   ← error in Java 9\r\n\r\n// Use descriptive names instead\r\nString unused = \"unused\";\r\nint ignored   = getValue();\r\n\r\n// (In Java 21, _ is a proper unnamed variable pattern)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "12ccfdda-a638-4634-b6ec-101b2f638b95",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Arrays API changes",
